OHOS: run statically linked programs untracked and keep their tasks out of the cache.

Tracking a statically linked program needs seccomp user-notification, and
HongMeng rejects SECCOMP_RET_USER_NOTIF (the pre_exec hook fails with EINVAL).
Without this patch, exec'ing a static child from a tracked task fails, and so
does spawning a task whose root command is static.

The pre_exec hook is skipped on OHOS (in the preload for children, in fspy for
the root command), and the loss is reported on the fspy channel by sending a
record too large for any frame: the channel refuses the claim and sets its
CLOSED gate, which vt already turns into TrackingIncomplete, so the task runs
but is not cached. Otherwise the child's file reads would be missing from the
trace and the cache would never be invalidated by them.

The Oversized record exists in both fspy and fspy_preload_unix because the
two crates do not depend on each other. Applies on top of 0003.

